# Renewal

Every membership ends at the close of its fiscal year. Renew it to continue for the following fiscal year.

Administrators can renew memberships manually from an individual membership page or from the "Renewals" section below the filters on [the memberships page](/memberships). You can also email renewal requests to all members, who can then renew or terminate their membership from a form in their account.

## Prerequisites {#prerequisites}

Before renewing memberships, create all [deliveries](/deliveries/new) for the new fiscal year (see [Deliveries](/handbook/deliveries)). If needed, update prices for the following year, including <%= BasketSize.model_name.human.downcase %>, <%= BasketComplement.model_name.human.downcase %>, and deposits. Renewal creates a new membership for the next fiscal year with the current membership's information.

### Default prices {#catalog-prices}

A price change on a <%= BasketSize.model_name.human.downcase %>, <%= BasketComplement.model_name.human.downcase %>, or depot applies to **new** memberships and to the **next** renewal. It does not rewrite memberships that already exist, including ones you already renewed for next year. Change those default prices **before** you renew. After that, edit the memberships (or [ask support](/support) for a bulk update).

Once the deliveries are created, administrators can renew memberships manually, at the time of their choice. Note that if a membership is renewed after the first delivery of the new fiscal year, that delivery will be included in the renewed membership regardless. That still holds if you send requests after the previous fiscal year has already closed.

### Fiscal year {#fiscal-year}

The fiscal year is the period configured in [the settings](/settings), not necessarily January to December. A winter delivery in January can still belong to the fiscal year that started the previous spring.

Create deliveries **only** for the next fiscal year. If you also create the year after that, the renewal form and the "Renew X memberships" button target that extra year. Members then think they are signing two years at once, and the "Renewals" section on [the memberships page](/memberships) asks for those extra deliveries. Delete the extra year: the Renewals section comes back for the year you actually meant.

## Sending requests {#sending-requests}

Once the prerequisites below are met, use the "Renewals" section below the filters on [the memberships page](/memberships):
![memberships section](<%= image_url("handbook/membership_renewal/section.en.png") %>){:class="small"}

> Renewal requests are not sent automatically. Choose when to send them according to your statutes or regulations. <br/><br/>
> If members do not respond, use the "Renew X memberships" button on [the memberships page](/memberships) to renew their memberships tacitly, or leave them unrenewed.

### Prerequisites

To send renewal requests, first set up:

- Create all [the deliveries](/deliveries/new) for the new fiscal year.
- Edit and activate [the "Membership Renewal" email template](/mail_templates/membership_renewal).
- Edit and activate [the "Membership Renewal (Reminder)" email template](/mail_templates/membership_renewal_reminder) (optional).
- Edit [the settings](/settings#membership_renewal), such as the explanation text displayed on the member page (requires "maximum" permission).

### Test sending a request

Once the prerequisites are met, send a renewal request to one member (for example, yourself) from their membership page to confirm that everything works as expected.

### Reminder email

When you set the "Send a reminder after (in days)" field in [the settings](/settings#membership_renewal), the system sends a reminder email X days after the renewal request to every member who has not yet renewed or terminated their membership.

[The "Membership Renewal (Reminder)" email template](/mail_templates/membership_renewal_reminder) must also have been edited and activated beforehand.

> As renewing or terminating memberships only makes sense before the first delivery of the new fiscal year, make sure there is always enough time between sending the reminder and this deadline.

## Renewal form {#renewal-form}

Once the renewal request is sent, the member can use a form on their membership page to renew or terminate their membership:

![memberships section](<%= image_url("handbook/membership_renewal/form.en.png") %>)

### Renewal

Members who choose to renew are redirected to a page where they can change their <%= BasketSize.model_name.human.downcase %>, <%= BasketComplement.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %> (if available), payment interval, and add a comment.

The following options are also available on the renewal page depending on your configuration:

- **Depot**: Members can change their depot if the "Allow depot change on renewal" option is enabled in [the settings](/settings#membership_renewal).
- **<%= Basket.model_name.human %> price extra**: Members can adjust their [extra price](/handbook/basket_price_extra) contribution.
- **<%= activities_human_name %>**: If a minimum and/or maximum number of participations is configured in [the settings](/settings#activity), members can adjust the number of requested participations within those bounds.

Once confirmed, their membership for the following fiscal year is automatically created and can be consulted and modified from the administration interface like any other membership. In case of error, the membership can be easily deleted, which will cancel the renewal.

### Configurations carried over {#carried-over}

When a membership is renewed (whether by the member or by an admin), certain configurations from the current membership are carried into the new one. The core configurations — <%= BasketSize.model_name.human.downcase %>, <%= BasketComplement.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %>, depot, delivery cycle, payment interval, and <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> price extra — are always carried over.

Additional configurations can be optionally carried over, controlled by the "Configurations carried over" checkboxes in [the settings](/settings#membership_renewal):

- **<%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2) %> price adjustment**: The custom price adjustment on <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %>.
- **<%= BasketComplement.model_name.human(count: 2) %> price adjustment**: The custom price adjustment on complements.
- **<%= activities_human_name %>**: The number of requested participations and any associated price adjustment.
- **Absences included annually**: The number of included absences (if different from the delivery cycle default).

If an attribute is not selected, it resets to the default value for the new membership. Price adjustments are also automatically cleared when the corresponding configuration changes (e.g., switching to a different <%= BasketSize.model_name.human.downcase %>).

### Termination

If the member chooses to terminate their membership, they will then be redirected to the termination page which will allow them to leave a free comment as well as choose to continue supporting the association as a supporting member by paying the annual fee (if applicable).

For administrators, the membership page separates several actions:

- **Cancel**: keeps the membership active until the end of the fiscal year, but excludes it from the renewal process. Automatic invoices for the next fiscal year stop; the current year still bills as configured.
- **Cancel (support)**: does the same, then keeps the member as a support member once the membership ends.
- **Stop**: ends the membership today; use the edit form instead if it must end on a specific date. Remaining invoices follow the [price change](/handbook/billing#price-change) rules on the next billing day.
- **Delete**: should only be used to correct a mistake, as it deletes the membership and deletes or cancels related invoices.

If needed, an administrator can reverse a membership termination from its membership page.
